1
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:11,667
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:32,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,900
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:41,100
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:44,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,033
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,533
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,000
- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]

10
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:53,767
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:55,633
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,133
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,133 --> 00:01:00,233
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,967 --> 00:01:03,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,733 --> 00:01:08,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,600
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,067
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

18
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:14,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:19,633 --> 00:01:21,533
<i>What use are you
if you can't issue</i>

20
00:01:21,533 --> 00:01:23,167
<i> a TRO against the demolition?</i>

21
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:25,733
<i>The people from Ginintuang
Lupa have already signed!</i>

22
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:27,467
- [LAUGHS]
-  Betchay, is that you?

23
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:28,600
<i> What's that, sardines?</i>

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,167
<i>These are imported!
They're corned beef!</i>

25
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:33,400
<i>I'm going to go around
our neighborhood</i>

26
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:34,933
<i> to get even more trash.</i>

27
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:36,733
<i>- Here's the tricycle.
- Let's get it.</i>

28
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:39,667
[SCREAMING]  Aah!

29
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:41,300
<i> It's on his face!</i>

30
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:43,067
<i>- [LOUD SLAP]
- [GRUNTS]</i>

31
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:44,367
<i> Good morning, Secretary.</i>

32
00:01:44,367 --> 00:01:46,000
<i>- Have you found anyone?
- This is Gabo.</i>

33
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,733
<i>He still has many trials
to go through</i>

34
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,800
<i>before we present him
to the president.</i>

35
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,433
<i> Your job has a lot of risks.</i>

36
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:55,300
<i>Your entire family
will be sacrificed.</i>

37
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,100
<i>I accept the mission to become
a member of Anino.</i>

38
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,433
<i>Someone needs to take action,
and that's me.</i>

39
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:05,400
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

40
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,667
[RUDY CLEARS THROAT]

41
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,100
[RUDY] Betchay.

42
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:19,867
Why don't you sleep next
to those so you won't lose it?

43
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:22,333
No, I want it
displayed right there

44
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:25,600
so there's
a nice sight to look at.

45
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,767
Your liver might get damaged.

46
00:02:27,767 --> 00:02:31,200
I don't care as long
as the food is delicious.

47
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,667
Is this all yours?

48
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:36,600
There's one for you.

49
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:37,700
[CAN THUDS]

50
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:41,100
Is this all?

51
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,033
Betchay.

52
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:44,333
Thank you so much.

53
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:47,767
We owe you
a lot for remembering us.

54
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:51,667
You're welcome.
You might say I'm being selfish.

55
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:53,600
Sure.

56
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:56,300
You're keeping all
the imported food to yourself.

57
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,000
And you dare to be picky?

58
00:02:58,333 --> 00:03:00,733
That's the only thing
that suits you!

59
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:01,900
[RUDY] Hold on, Betchay.

60
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:03,733
Where did you get these?!

61
00:03:03,733 --> 00:03:05,500
And don't you think
this is too much?

62
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:07,433
You're acting like
it's going to run out

63
00:03:07,433 --> 00:03:08,633
Did you win the lottery?

64
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,700
You guys are something else.

65
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,767
Can't it be that I broke
my back working hard,

66
00:03:13,767 --> 00:03:15,933
which is how I was able
to buy something like that?

67
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:19,367
It's because you're lazy,
that's why you don't get it.

68
00:03:19,367 --> 00:03:20,567
You're lazy.

69
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:22,233
Oh, you know what,

70
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:25,033
you should pray
that Gabo gets the job.

71
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:27,100
What does Gabo have
to do with all of this?

72
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:32,100
Because once he gets a job
and becomes successful,

73
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:35,633
ou guys will finally be able
to buy imported stuff too.

74
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:42,667
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

75
00:03:44,133 --> 00:03:47,000
It's a good thing that
we broke away from that.

76
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:50,633
I'm getting irritated
by that woman's face!

77
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,733
It's actually great. We'll have
a lot of things to scavenge.

78
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:56,200
I don't want to do that
anymore. Let them get tired.

79
00:03:56,233 --> 00:03:57,767
Why did we even agree
to clean up

80
00:03:57,767 --> 00:03:59,500
around here
in the first place?

81
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,433
[TOLITS] Fair point.

82
00:04:02,433 --> 00:04:04,533
You're allergic to cleanliness.

83
00:04:04,533 --> 00:04:07,467
When we were kids, if you
were assigned as a cleaner,

84
00:04:07,467 --> 00:04:10,333
all you did was clap
the blackboard erasers,

85
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,867
then after a few minutes,
you're already at home.

86
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:15,100
- [LAUGHTER]
- You're great, aren't you?

87
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,567
At a young age,
you were already so bossy.

88
00:04:16,567 --> 00:04:19,933
See? That's called being smart.

89
00:04:19,933 --> 00:04:21,733
And besides,
with a beauty like mine,

90
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:24,200
you're just going to make me
pick up trash? Gross!

91
00:04:24,733 --> 00:04:26,067
You talk too much.

92
00:04:26,067 --> 00:04:27,500
- Why did you come along?
- Yeah!

93
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,933
You told me to come back!

94
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:30,367
- Oh, yeah.
- See?

95
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:32,433
If Gabo finds out
you didn't help,

96
00:04:32,433 --> 00:04:33,733
that's minus points for you!

97
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:35,133
You'll have to settle for Daboy.

98
00:04:35,133 --> 00:04:37,300
What are you guys
still waiting for?

99
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,233
Go find something
we can pitch in on

100
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:41,233
so we won't get
called out for not contributing.

101
00:04:41,233 --> 00:04:42,500
[LAUGHS]

102
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,000
This person's selfishness
is right down to the bone.

103
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,200
Hey, hey, hey!

104
00:04:46,567 --> 00:04:48,400
If you guys only knew
what's in my heart

105
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:49,533
and how much
resentment I'm holding,

106
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:51,000
it's me who's been
taken advantage of!

107
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,867
Hmm. Let's go.

108
00:04:52,867 --> 00:04:54,667
You don't care about the Earth.

109
00:04:54,667 --> 00:04:57,433
I don't care about you,
so pick that trash up already!

110
00:04:57,433 --> 00:04:58,933
[SAM] Let's go!

111
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:00,133
Here!

112
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,900
- There's cardboard here.
- Here!

113
00:05:01,933 --> 00:05:03,367
That's a waste.

114
00:05:03,367 --> 00:05:04,667
I think there's more over there.

115
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:07,100
- Let's go.
- Are you guys okay?

116
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,300
Let's go.

117
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:10,167
Wow!

118
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:12,067
Did you pick up a lot?

119
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,300
Mm-hmm.
Tarpaulins and bottles.

120
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:17,767
Wow! You guys are so good!

121
00:05:17,767 --> 00:05:19,300
What about you?
Where's yours?

122
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:21,333
You guys don't seem to be tired.

123
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:23,733
We're actually so tired! See!

124
00:05:24,133 --> 00:05:25,400
These were so hard to fine!

125
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:28,267
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:05:28,267 --> 00:05:30,167
What are yours,
Tolits and Tekla?

127
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,067
[TEKLA] There! There it is!

128
00:05:32,067 --> 00:05:33,633
We worked together to find that.

129
00:05:33,633 --> 00:05:34,633
I've put it together.

130
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:35,733
Are you serious? Is that it?

131
00:05:36,267 --> 00:05:37,167
- Yes.
- Yes.

132
00:05:37,933 --> 00:05:39,333
[SCOFFS] Thanks.

133
00:05:39,767 --> 00:05:42,000
- You're welcome.
- Did you really pick up trash?

134
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,600
It looks like you didn't!

135
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:44,900
You're being too harsh!

136
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,733
We didn't see that much trash!

137
00:05:46,733 --> 00:05:47,900
[CHUCKLES SARCASTICALLY]

138
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:50,000
You really think there's
no trash in Ginintuang Lupa?

139
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,367
You're lying to us again.

140
00:05:52,367 --> 00:05:54,400
You're suspecting us
over trash?!

141
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:58,067
Even if you check the CCTVs
of the alleyways we went into,

142
00:05:58,067 --> 00:05:59,933
you'll see how exhausted
we were!

143
00:05:59,933 --> 00:06:00,933
What are you talking about?

144
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:04,067
There are no CCTVs here!

145
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:07,833
What we have in our place
is thieves and trash.

146
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:10,000
Hey, watch what you're saying!

147
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,833
We're not lying!
You can smell Tolits for proof!

148
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:14,233
See? He smells like body odor!

149
00:06:14,233 --> 00:06:16,833
[TOLITS] Dude, we're talking
about trash, not my smell.

150
00:06:16,833 --> 00:06:19,200
C'mon, so we can prove it!

151
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,800
That's enough.

152
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,767
Let's go.

153
00:06:22,367 --> 00:06:24,200
- Let's go.
- Those are easy to find!

154
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,733
The trash we found
is easy to find!

155
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:28,433
You can even sell it to boss...

156
00:06:28,433 --> 00:06:29,400
[DIDAY] Rosa!

157
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,867
The drainage canals
are clean now!

158
00:06:31,367 --> 00:06:32,567
Thank you!

159
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:34,900
- Look at you.
- [RUDY] Gloria!

160
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,367
- Pa.
- Come, guys.

161
00:06:37,633 --> 00:06:39,033
[ELTON] Looks like you guys
got a lot, huh!

162
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,300
Yes. We're tired,
but we had fun, right?

163
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:43,867
- Yes.
- Oh, no.

164
00:06:43,867 --> 00:06:45,133
I just got tired.

165
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:47,933
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:06:47,933 --> 00:06:49,133
- Oh.
- Can I have some?

167
00:06:49,133 --> 00:06:50,867
[TOLITS] The mega star
is mad again.

168
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:55,633
Elton, we got a pedicab
from the dumpsite,

169
00:06:55,633 --> 00:06:57,033
it's a bit damaged.

170
00:06:57,033 --> 00:06:59,167
Please fix it
so Gloria can use it.

171
00:07:00,167 --> 00:07:01,467
You could easily fix that.

172
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:04,433
It looks alright.

173
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:08,233
Leave it.
We'll take care of it.

174
00:07:08,233 --> 00:07:09,400
Wait a minute.

175
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,200
Are you sure this isn't stolen?

176
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:13,267
[CHUCKLES]

177
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:14,600
- C'mon, Rudy.
- Rudy!

178
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,433
This has been discarded.

179
00:07:17,433 --> 00:07:20,000
We just adopted it.
We didn't steal it.

180
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,067
That's good.

181
00:07:21,267 --> 00:07:24,133
Pa, Elton,

182
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:27,567
please fix it so we can
use it to get more garbage.

183
00:07:27,567 --> 00:07:30,333
- She's right.
- That's why we took it.

184
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,500
Leave it to me and Rudy.

185
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,500
We'll work on it in a while.

186
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:35,633
Okay. Thank you!

187
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,267
Let's bring everything down.

188
00:07:37,267 --> 00:07:39,200
- Let's put these down!
- Put those down.

189
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:41,133
- Be careful.
- Move! Move!

190
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,500
- Here.
- Here.

191
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,933
You can handle that,
look at how big you are!

192
00:07:44,933 --> 00:07:47,233
- Leave it to us, Gloria!
- I'll leave it to you, guys.

193
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:49,367
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

194
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:52,567
Pa, I just remembered Gabo.
I wonder how he's doing.

195
00:07:52,567 --> 00:07:54,600
I wonder how
his job search is going.

196
00:07:55,233 --> 00:07:57,133
Dear, don't worry about him.

197
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:59,700
I raised Gabo to be resourceful.

198
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:03,100
When he comes home, he'll
surely have a surprise for you.

199
00:08:04,467 --> 00:08:06,000
I really hope he's fine.

200
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,433
Oh, by the way, look at this.

201
00:08:08,433 --> 00:08:09,667
There.

202
00:08:09,667 --> 00:08:13,800
We've already started building
the junk shop for your project.

203
00:08:14,667 --> 00:08:16,900
Oh Pa! You didn't have
to do that!

204
00:08:17,433 --> 00:08:18,633
Thank you.

205
00:08:18,633 --> 00:08:20,800
Don't mention it!
It's just a little help

206
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,300
from me and your Uncle Dante.

207
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:26,667
You can now put the trash
you got in there!

208
00:08:26,667 --> 00:08:28,633
That's now clean and tidy.

209
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:31,300
- Thank you.
- Gloria.

210
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,767
- You're here.
- [GLORIA] Uncle! Thank you!

211
00:08:33,767 --> 00:08:36,467
We're finishing up
your junk shop.

212
00:08:36,467 --> 00:08:37,633
Looks good, right?

213
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:39,600
Thank you, really.

214
00:08:40,467 --> 00:08:41,767
I'm just going to make
rounds again. I'll be back.

215
00:08:42,067 --> 00:08:44,000
- Okay. Finish that.
- Sure, sure.

216
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,633
Oh, where are you going?

217
00:08:45,633 --> 00:08:47,367
I'll go to the kitchen!

218
00:08:47,367 --> 00:08:49,500
- Be quick!
- Yes!

219
00:08:50,933 --> 00:08:53,267
Come, I'm going
to show you something.

220
00:08:53,267 --> 00:09:00,267
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:06,667
[PIANO KEYS PLAYING]

222
00:09:14,067 --> 00:09:16,000
Come, Gabo. Follow me.

223
00:09:18,467 --> 00:09:22,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:09:22,567 --> 00:09:26,333
Like what we told you
during your training,

225
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:30,500
you can use all these cars
for your missions.

226
00:09:31,167 --> 00:09:35,333
Not every mission
is the same, Gabo.

227
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:38,533
There are places where
you need to be quick.

228
00:09:38,533 --> 00:09:42,800
There are places where you
need to blend in with the crowd.

229
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,733
With the right car,

230
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:50,100
you can easily
defeat your opponent.

231
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:54,000
That is the car you'll use
for your next mission, Gabo.

232
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,600
The entire car is
bullet resistant.

233
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,900
It has hybrid armor,

234
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:05,600
with harness steel covered
with light ballistic composite

235
00:10:05,633 --> 00:10:08,633
to make it sturdy
without making it heavy.

236
00:10:08,633 --> 00:10:13,000
Even the windows are made
with layered ballistic glass.

237
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:17,367
It has military-grade tires,
high-tech built-in radio,

238
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:21,367
reinforced with Ironhead fibers
to make it sturdy.

239
00:10:21,367 --> 00:10:25,633
This cab is equipped with the
latest security, communication,

240
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:28,033
navigation and
surveillance systems.

241
00:10:28,033 --> 00:10:30,367
It also has instant throttle.

242
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:32,933
Once you hit the gas,
the power is there.

243
00:10:32,933 --> 00:10:36,100
There are also built-in
weapons and equipment

244
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:40,100
that can help you escape
and for your protection.

245
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:43,433
You have the choice
to flee or fight.

246
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:45,400
It has six loads.

247
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:48,367
No one can steal this car.

248
00:10:48,933 --> 00:10:50,400
Sick!

249
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,033
Feels like I'm James Bond!

250
00:10:52,033 --> 00:10:53,333
This is dope!

251
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:55,367
- It's beautiful!
- [PAPANG LAUGHS]

252
00:10:56,467 --> 00:10:57,700
[PAPANG LAUGHS]

253
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,233
Even the glass is thick!

254
00:11:01,067 --> 00:11:02,133
Handsome!

255
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:06,333
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

256
00:11:12,767 --> 00:11:14,000
- [POT LID CLANKS]
- Let's see.

257
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,167
Oh, there's rice.

258
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,333
Wait...

259
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:19,500
[CAN CLATTERS]

260
00:11:22,467 --> 00:11:26,767
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

261
00:11:26,767 --> 00:11:28,867
I bet this one's better. Wait.

262
00:11:39,033 --> 00:11:40,100
There.

263
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:45,933
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

264
00:11:45,967 --> 00:11:46,933
[PLATES CLATTERING]

265
00:11:48,467 --> 00:11:49,800
[POT LID CLANKS]

266
00:11:54,167 --> 00:11:56,633
[CAN LID POPPING OPEN]

267
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:57,733
[THUDS]

268
00:12:01,467 --> 00:12:04,133
I'll just eat first. I'm hungry.

269
00:12:06,467 --> 00:12:10,000
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,033
Hmm! So delicious.

271
00:12:11,033 --> 00:12:12,000
[SAM] Alright.

272
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:14,300
What?

273
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:16,633
- Let's get started.
- [WOMAN 1] Sure.

274
00:12:16,633 --> 00:12:18,600
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

275
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,633
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

276
00:12:20,333 --> 00:12:22,400
Okay, here's what we'll do.

277
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,500
Can you get some scissors?

278
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,500
- I'll show you something.
- Oh, okay, sure.

279
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:30,000
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

280
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,300
[WOMAN 2] Here you go.

281
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,200
Okay, so here's what we'll do.

282
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:37,333
We can cut these lengthwise.

283
00:12:37,333 --> 00:12:38,467
- All of them.
- [WOMAN 3] Okay.

284
00:12:38,467 --> 00:12:40,133
Once we have enough strips,

285
00:12:40,133 --> 00:12:42,433
we can make a bag,
a coin purse.

286
00:12:42,433 --> 00:12:43,933
We'll just braid them together.

287
00:12:43,933 --> 00:12:45,333
- That's nice.
- Sound good?

288
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:46,467
Yes. Let's start.

289
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,600
Go ahead and get started.

290
00:12:48,633 --> 00:12:49,767
- Okay, sure.
- Alright.

291
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:52,200
We'll finally get
our revenge on them.

292
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:55,800
I'll cut out their faces.

293
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:58,200
They are so greedy.

294
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:00,567
Let's turn their faces
into coin purses.

295
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:03,733
- This is our chance.
- Especially you!

296
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:05,433
You're greedy for land.

297
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,333
Maybe I should turn you
into an eco-bag...

298
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:09,600
Alright, I'll be back.

299
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,867
...so it'll be useful
for something.

300
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:18,633
Madam Rosa,
I brought you a gift!

301
00:13:18,633 --> 00:13:20,833
- Wow!
- [CHUCKLES]

302
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:22,700
It's beautiful.

303
00:13:22,733 --> 00:13:27,267
Madam Rosa is happy
with your gift.

304
00:13:27,267 --> 00:13:29,200
- Hmm.
- I'm glad you liked it.

305
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:31,100
[GIGGLES] Hmm! Look--

306
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,167
Again?

307
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:34,300
[STUTTERS]

308
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:37,133
Okay, fine. I'll stay away now.

309
00:13:37,133 --> 00:13:38,567
I'll stay away.

310
00:13:44,067 --> 00:13:47,167
Pinky, have the Abads
been asking

311
00:13:47,167 --> 00:13:49,333
about Ginintuang Lupa
Development again?

312
00:13:49,333 --> 00:13:53,100
Actually, they've been
pestering me

313
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,533
for weeks now, Ricardo.

314
00:13:54,567 --> 00:14:00,200
I just told them you're dealing
with some personal issues.

315
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:03,833
Please tell them I'm doing
everything I can

316
00:14:04,333 --> 00:14:07,400
to fast-track the demolition
of that place.

317
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:11,533
But also tell them I appreciate
their understanding

318
00:14:11,533 --> 00:14:13,667
of what I'm going through
personally.

319
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:15,367
That's why I haven't been
able to focus on it.

320
00:14:15,367 --> 00:14:19,133
Well, I hope you'll understand

321
00:14:19,133 --> 00:14:25,067
that you shouldn't be focusing
on your business right now,

322
00:14:25,633 --> 00:14:29,467
especially when Sam just died.

323
00:14:30,033 --> 00:14:31,900
Isobel, what do you
want me to do?

324
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:35,633
Just sit here and listen to
all the garbage you're saying?

325
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:41,800
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,967
Excuse me.

327
00:14:43,867 --> 00:14:44,900
Ricardo.

328
00:14:45,933 --> 00:14:47,500
Ricardo!

329
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:51,867
My god!
You are so unbelievable!

330
00:14:51,867 --> 00:14:56,133
Is it really that easy for you
to dismiss Sam's death?!

331
00:14:56,133 --> 00:14:58,433
Isobel, I'm not dismissing it.

332
00:14:58,433 --> 00:15:01,300
I hate to say this,
but life goes on.

333
00:15:03,133 --> 00:15:04,767
As hard as it is to admit...

334
00:15:05,333 --> 00:15:08,133
we're still alive, and
we have to face that reality.

335
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:11,233
You couldn't even take a break,

336
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,300
reflect,

337
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,733
and realize that
if Sam were alive,

338
00:15:15,733 --> 00:15:17,667
she wouldn't want you
doing this,

339
00:15:17,667 --> 00:15:20,100
destroying Ginintuang Lupa!

340
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,067
But she's not alive
anymore, Isobel!

341
00:15:22,933 --> 00:15:24,133
And you know why?

342
00:15:24,467 --> 00:15:26,900
Because the people
of Ginintuang Lupa

343
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,867
didn't even help her
on the night she died!

344
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:32,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

345
00:15:32,333 --> 00:15:34,500
This isn't just about business.

346
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:38,767
That's not the only reason I
want Ginintuang Lupa demolished.

347
00:15:40,933 --> 00:15:42,200
This is personal.

348
00:15:43,733 --> 00:15:44,833
It's personal now!

349
00:15:44,833 --> 00:15:51,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,033
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:15:54,033 --> 00:15:55,767
Oh, is that everything?

352
00:15:55,767 --> 00:15:57,100
Okay, you can put those
in here now.

353
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,167
- Just move the rest over.
- Okay, sure.

354
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:00,667
- Alright.
- This looks good.

355
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:02,133
Let's check
this electric fan, too.

356
00:16:02,133 --> 00:16:04,433
Then we can put this one
in the back.

357
00:16:04,433 --> 00:16:06,333
- Okay, sure.
- What about this?

358
00:16:06,333 --> 00:16:07,533
Is it still working?

359
00:16:07,533 --> 00:16:14,533
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

360
00:16:29,267 --> 00:16:34,433
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

361
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,333
This is our main armory.

362
00:16:38,333 --> 00:16:39,700
- Go ahead and choose.
- [GUN COCKS]

363
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:42,300
We have all the guns
you might want to use.

364
00:16:44,333 --> 00:16:47,200
Encrypted,
military-grade phones.

365
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,333
Even without cellular signal,

366
00:16:49,333 --> 00:16:52,800
they'll automatically handshake
with low-orbit satellites.

367
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:55,000
They have iris scan
verification.

368
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,100
Only you can unlock them.

369
00:16:57,100 --> 00:17:01,167
They sync directly with the
vehicle's onboard computer.

370
00:17:01,167 --> 00:17:04,367
One device,
but it's a full command center.

371
00:17:04,367 --> 00:17:06,033
That's a tactical watch.

372
00:17:06,033 --> 00:17:09,333
It's integrated
with the car's AI system,

373
00:17:09,333 --> 00:17:11,433
so you can control it remotely.

374
00:17:11,433 --> 00:17:14,433
It has its own encrypted link
to the vehicle,

375
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:17,400
even when you don't have
your phone with you.

376
00:17:17,433 --> 00:17:20,567
Heavy-duty, shatterproof lenses.

377
00:17:20,567 --> 00:17:22,533
They have built-in night vision

378
00:17:22,533 --> 00:17:26,733
and an embedded encrypted
communications microcamera.

379
00:17:26,733 --> 00:17:31,700
Everything you see goes
straight to the car's AI system.

380
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:34,367
The firearms package
is compact,

381
00:17:34,367 --> 00:17:37,333
but it packs full-size
stopping power.

382
00:17:37,333 --> 00:17:39,433
High-caliber ammunition,

383
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:42,867
with terminal force
and reliability

384
00:17:42,867 --> 00:17:44,167
as the top priorities.

385
00:17:44,167 --> 00:17:45,333
dragon skin-inspired
ballistic fabric,

386
00:17:45,333 --> 00:17:47,033
The uniform is made
of dragon-skin-inspired

387
00:17:47,033 --> 00:17:48,700
ballistic fabric.

388
00:17:48,733 --> 00:17:51,933
It's multilayered,
with flexible armor.

389
00:17:51,933 --> 00:17:54,267
It has a temperature-adaptive
layer

390
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:58,633
that regulates heat depending
on the environment.

391
00:17:58,633 --> 00:18:01,667
The outer fabric
is also fire-resistant.

392
00:18:01,667 --> 00:18:04,700
Built for extreme conditions.

393
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:05,967
Go ahead and use those.

394
00:18:05,967 --> 00:18:08,133
I'll introduce you to Alex, too.

395
00:18:08,767 --> 00:18:10,367
- Alex?
- Yes. Get in.

396
00:18:10,367 --> 00:18:11,733
Alex will accompany you.

397
00:18:11,733 --> 00:18:13,467
Go on, get in. [CHUCKLES]

398
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,233
You'll get to know Alex.

399
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:20,133
Alex, I'd like you to meet Gabo.

400
00:18:20,133 --> 00:18:22,500
Take good care of him, okay?

401
00:18:22,533 --> 00:18:23,767
I'll leave him in your hands.

402
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:26,333
- Wow, this is really high-tech.
- I'll leave him to you, Alex!

403
00:18:26,333 --> 00:18:27,433
[ALEX]  Okay, Pops.

404
00:18:27,433 --> 00:18:31,167
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

405
00:18:31,167 --> 00:18:32,833
[ALEX]  Good morning, Gabo.

406
00:18:32,833 --> 00:18:34,767
[GABO] Good morning, Alex!

407
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:37,767
<i>Gabo, you need to wear
your seat belt.</i>

408
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,367
Oh...

409
00:18:41,033 --> 00:18:42,300
[PAPANG] Alex...

410
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:46,567
Adaptive Logistics
and Execution.

411
00:18:46,567 --> 00:18:49,633
Alex will be your primary system

412
00:18:49,633 --> 00:18:51,200
while you're on the road.

413
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:55,133
Alex will handle navigation,
communication, surveillance,

414
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:59,067
and any other systems
you'll need for your mission.

415
00:18:59,067 --> 00:19:02,167
Alex is connected to the taxi,
your watch,

416
00:19:02,167 --> 00:19:05,133
your earpiece,
and your shades.

417
00:19:05,133 --> 00:19:08,700
Just tell Alex what you need.

418
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:11,967
You and the vehicle are one.

419
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:16,467
- [CAR ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

420
00:19:16,467 --> 00:19:18,367
Awesome! This is so high-tech!

421
00:19:18,367 --> 00:19:18,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

422
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:21,800
[MAMENG] Dante!

423
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,933
- Hmm?
- [MAMENG] Help me with these.

424
00:19:23,933 --> 00:19:25,367
Oh.

425
00:19:25,367 --> 00:19:27,400
You're home, babe.
Hold on.

426
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:31,467
- Here.
- You bought a lot.

427
00:19:31,467 --> 00:19:32,800
Is this what
we're going to cook?

428
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,067
Yeah. Bring them in.

429
00:19:34,067 --> 00:19:34,900
Okay.

430
00:19:40,667 --> 00:19:42,533
What are you eating?

431
00:19:42,533 --> 00:19:43,667
Oh, it's delicious.

432
00:19:43,667 --> 00:19:46,867
I'm sick of eating
canned sardines.

433
00:19:46,867 --> 00:19:47,767
What were you thinking, Dante?

434
00:19:47,767 --> 00:19:49,033
Betchay bought that!

435
00:19:49,033 --> 00:19:51,000
- So?
- What do you mean by "So"?

436
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,767
You knew I was going
to the market.

437
00:19:52,767 --> 00:19:54,333
You could've waited for me
to get back.

438
00:19:54,333 --> 00:19:55,833
This is so good.

439
00:19:55,833 --> 00:19:58,167
I haven't had
luncheon meat in a while.

440
00:19:58,167 --> 00:20:00,133
- Come on.
- You are unbelievable.

441
00:20:00,133 --> 00:20:02,633
She's going to find out
you ate her food.

442
00:20:02,667 --> 00:20:04,733
Listen, if Betchay asks me
who ate it,

443
00:20:04,733 --> 00:20:06,300
I'm not covering for you.

444
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:07,933
Don't worry.

445
00:20:07,933 --> 00:20:09,233
I have a plan.

446
00:20:09,233 --> 00:20:11,033
I'll put back the empty can
where I got it from.

447
00:20:11,033 --> 00:20:14,600
Then, before she realizes
the can is empty,

448
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,367
I'll get ahead of her.

449
00:20:16,367 --> 00:20:18,067
- Wow.
- Look.

450
00:20:18,067 --> 00:20:20,667
Just like that.

451
00:20:20,667 --> 00:20:22,233
- See?
- Right...

452
00:20:22,233 --> 00:20:25,000
As if she wouldn't notice that.

453
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,867
Just help me cook.

454
00:20:28,867 --> 00:20:31,433
- Let me finish this.
- Oh, whatever.

455
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:34,133
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

456
00:20:34,133 --> 00:20:35,200
All done.

457
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:36,867
Mm.

458
00:20:36,867 --> 00:20:38,667
- Stop that.
- How's it going here?

459
00:20:38,667 --> 00:20:40,800
- We've finished some already.
- Doing great!

460
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:43,767
You're going to like this.
Where should we put it?

461
00:20:43,767 --> 00:20:47,033
"DO NOT THROW GARBAGE HERE.
YOU WILL BE SHOT.

462
00:20:47,033 --> 00:20:49,200
IF YOU SURVIVE,
YOU WILL BE SHOT AGAIN!"

463
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:50,333
There's no escape!

464
00:20:50,333 --> 00:20:51,333
Jeez, guys.

465
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,300
"DO NOT THROW GARBAGE HERE"
would do.

466
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:55,167
The rest is unnecessary.

467
00:20:55,167 --> 00:20:56,833
People won't follow this
if they're not afraid!

468
00:20:56,833 --> 00:20:58,767
- Oh, don't be silly.
- Come on, man.

469
00:20:58,767 --> 00:21:00,933
"HAND OVER YOUR GARBAGE"
Like this, right, Gloria?

470
00:21:00,933 --> 00:21:02,167
- Yeah, sure.
- [TOLITS] Here's mine.

471
00:21:02,167 --> 00:21:03,967
"I'LL HANDLE YOUR TRASH!"

472
00:21:03,967 --> 00:21:05,167
- Yeah.
- [BONG] Listen to this.

473
00:21:05,167 --> 00:21:06,367
"YOU HAVE A BETTER CHANCE OF
FINDING A FUTURE IN THE TRASH

474
00:21:06,367 --> 00:21:07,867
THAN WITH YOUR LOVER."

475
00:21:07,867 --> 00:21:08,933
- Yeah!
- That's the stuff!

476
00:21:08,967 --> 00:21:10,467
- Mine's awesome.
- Yeah?

477
00:21:10,467 --> 00:21:12,500
"LOOKING FOR GARBAGE"

478
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,933
- Am I looking for you?
- [EXCLAIMS, LAUGHS]

479
00:21:14,933 --> 00:21:16,767
[IN SING-SONG VOICE]
Looking for garbage!

480
00:21:16,767 --> 00:21:18,067
Okay, all right.
Keep it up, boys.

481
00:21:18,067 --> 00:21:19,700
You've done a lot.

482
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:22,233
- I drew you.
- Don't sniff it!

483
00:21:22,233 --> 00:21:23,700
[DABOY] That looks horrible!

484
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:25,167
You wouldn't stay still.

485
00:21:25,167 --> 00:21:26,600
- I'll go look around.
- Okay.

486
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:28,900
- Keep it up.
- All right.

487
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:30,367
- Hey, Elton.
- [ELTON] Hmm?

488
00:21:30,367 --> 00:21:32,567
Fix the chain, all right?

489
00:21:32,567 --> 00:21:34,100
Then pump some air into this.

490
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:37,700
- The wheel's still deflated.
- I got it.

491
00:21:39,067 --> 00:21:40,100
[RUDY] Good.

492
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:44,900
- [WATER RUNNING]
- [PLATES, UTENSILS CLATTERING]

493
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:47,100
- [BETCHAY CLEARS THROAT]
- [PLATE CLATTERS]

494
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:06,667
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

495
00:22:14,633 --> 00:22:17,533
Who ate this?

496
00:22:17,567 --> 00:22:19,267
Did you cook this?

497
00:22:19,267 --> 00:22:21,267
Did you, Dante?

498
00:22:21,267 --> 00:22:23,700
Don't shake your head
like some bobblehead dog!

499
00:22:23,700 --> 00:22:25,000
Answer me!

500
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:28,500
Can't you see
I'm only drinking water?

501
00:22:30,167 --> 00:22:32,400
What's that?
That's oil.

502
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:34,900
Ah! It smells like
imported luncheon meat!

503
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:37,400
You! You cooked my
imported luncheon meat!

504
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,100
And you lied about it!

505
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:40,200
You're a thief.

506
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,333
I shouldn't be surprised.

507
00:22:41,333 --> 00:22:45,867
Thieves and liars are one
and the same nowadays!

508
00:22:45,867 --> 00:22:47,067
So what if I ate it?

509
00:22:47,067 --> 00:22:48,733
It was in our kitchen!

510
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:50,200
It's mine!

511
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:53,733
- So is this.
- [CAN CLATTERS]

512
00:22:53,733 --> 00:22:58,967
- And this, and this, and this.
- [CANS CLATTERING]

513
00:22:58,967 --> 00:23:01,400
And all of these!
They're all mine!

514
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:03,200
You disgust me!

515
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,167
Pig!

516
00:23:05,167 --> 00:23:07,100
I'm coming back
for the rest!

517
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:08,233
You can have 'em all!

518
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:14,233
Unbelievable.

519
00:23:14,233 --> 00:23:17,567
These people are animals!

520
00:23:17,567 --> 00:23:20,567
I know every single item
I bought!

521
00:23:20,567 --> 00:23:25,000
Every single one!
You hear me?

522
00:23:25,033 --> 00:23:27,467
They better not eat another one.

523
00:23:27,467 --> 00:23:29,500
Because I'll know!

524
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:34,900
If you dare to do that again,
you'll regret it!

525
00:23:35,967 --> 00:23:37,667
One, two...

526
00:23:37,667 --> 00:23:39,267
Did I leave any behind?

527
00:23:39,267 --> 00:23:40,767
No, only two cans are left.

528
00:23:40,767 --> 00:23:47,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

529
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:52,133
Raul Montero.

530
00:23:52,133 --> 00:23:54,233
That's your first target.

531
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,433
He's not easy to track, either.

532
00:23:58,300 --> 00:24:00,533
[TOMAS] He has multiple bases.

533
00:24:00,533 --> 00:24:01,800
He never stays
in the same location,

534
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:04,167
so tracking him is impossible.

535
00:24:04,167 --> 00:24:06,767
That's his last-known location.

536
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:11,400
[OMENG]
It's an abandoned property.

537
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,833
So we were able to keep it
under surveillance.

538
00:24:13,833 --> 00:24:17,667
There is no confirmation
that he is still using the site.

539
00:24:17,667 --> 00:24:20,733
It's unclear where
he moved his base.

540
00:24:20,733 --> 00:24:23,667
[UWAK] There are other areas
we are trying to keep an eye on.

541
00:24:23,667 --> 00:24:25,733
The people staying there
are never the same.

542
00:24:26,467 --> 00:24:27,967
Sometimes,
no one arrives at all.

543
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:30,133
We have a number of locations

544
00:24:30,167 --> 00:24:32,767
that will give us
information about him.

545
00:24:32,767 --> 00:24:34,667
[PAPANG] However,
we can't be sure if

546
00:24:34,667 --> 00:24:36,933
he's still using that location.

547
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:39,600
[OMENG]
We've gathered evidence

548
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:43,867
that gives us an idea
of what they're doing.

549
00:24:43,867 --> 00:24:50,833
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

550
00:24:51,500 --> 00:24:53,167
[OMENG] Based on
the information I have gathered,

551
00:24:53,167 --> 00:24:57,933
they target women with
little to no sexual experience.

552
00:24:57,933 --> 00:25:01,633
It's what foreign customers
are demanding.

553
00:25:01,633 --> 00:25:03,667
They're not prostitutes.

554
00:25:03,700 --> 00:25:06,200
They don't know
what they were getting into.

555
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,567
Some were recruited,
while others were approached.

556
00:25:09,567 --> 00:25:11,433
Others are missing persons.

557
00:25:11,433 --> 00:25:13,700
[OMENG] It doesn't end there.

558
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:16,267
[PAPANG] These are only
reported cases, Gabo.

559
00:25:16,267 --> 00:25:18,200
That doesn't include
the cases that

560
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:21,367
never reported
to the authorities.

561
00:25:21,367 --> 00:25:25,233
[OMENG] The money goes through
different accounts.

562
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:26,733
It's constantly
being transferred,

563
00:25:26,733 --> 00:25:28,567
making it untraceable.

564
00:25:28,567 --> 00:25:31,133
[TOMAS] There are
foreign nationals involved

565
00:25:31,133 --> 00:25:33,700
who invest in the network.

566
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:37,267
[GABO] It means this problem
goes beyond our country.

567
00:25:37,300 --> 00:25:38,600
Yes.

568
00:25:41,267 --> 00:25:43,700
How do they approach
these women?

569
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:46,867
They are all connected
to the same person:

570
00:25:46,867 --> 00:25:48,300
Misty Manalo.

571
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:51,667
[OMENG] She doesn't have
a criminal record

572
00:25:51,667 --> 00:25:55,467
or a paper trail
connecting her to the network.

573
00:25:55,467 --> 00:25:58,933
She is constantly seen
in the photographs

574
00:25:58,933 --> 00:26:00,667
of the women
who go missing.

575
00:26:00,667 --> 00:26:02,333
[OMENG] And we can't confirm

576
00:26:02,333 --> 00:26:03,767
what role she plays
in this operation.

577
00:26:03,767 --> 00:26:06,633
Misty is currently in Manila.

578
00:26:06,633 --> 00:26:08,767
It looks like she's
recruiting new victims.

579
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:10,233
[TOMAS] That's where
she was last seen.

580
00:26:10,233 --> 00:26:13,200
You have to keep
an eye on her, Gabo.

581
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:15,200
[PAPANG]
Don't just follow her.

582
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:18,667
Watch her carefully.
Find out what she's doing.

583
00:26:18,667 --> 00:26:20,800
[GABO] How can being
a taxi driver help me

584
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:21,833
with my mission?

585
00:26:22,533 --> 00:26:26,600
Misty is associated with
a high-end modeling agency.

586
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:28,467
She moves from
place to place.

587
00:26:28,467 --> 00:26:31,833
She often visits
high-end establishments

588
00:26:31,833 --> 00:26:35,100
where she can meet
and recruit women.

589
00:26:35,100 --> 00:26:37,900
We don't have
enough information

590
00:26:37,900 --> 00:26:39,967
to determine her exact role
in the network.

591
00:26:39,967 --> 00:26:42,133
You need to focus on her.

592
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:44,633
Go to the places she goes to.

593
00:26:44,633 --> 00:26:46,733
According to
the initial investigation,

594
00:26:46,733 --> 00:26:51,433
Misty gets around by taxi.

595
00:26:52,567 --> 00:26:55,533
And that's where
you come in, Gabo.

596
00:26:55,533 --> 00:26:58,200
[UWAK] She doesn't need to
be your passenger.

597
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:01,367
You just need to be
where she is.

598
00:27:01,367 --> 00:27:03,967
[OMENG] We uploaded the profiles

599
00:27:03,967 --> 00:27:06,100
of Raul Montero
and Misty Manalo,

600
00:27:06,100 --> 00:27:07,833
as well as those
of the confirmed victims,

601
00:27:07,833 --> 00:27:09,300
to Alex's memory.

602
00:27:09,300 --> 00:27:11,067
As well as Misty's photo.

603
00:27:11,067 --> 00:27:14,633
Your priority is
to gain her trust.

604
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:17,233
Get close. Observe.

605
00:27:17,267 --> 00:27:19,300
Learn more about her.

606
00:27:19,300 --> 00:27:22,633
Find out who the people
she interacts with are

607
00:27:22,633 --> 00:27:25,167
and where they go.

608
00:27:25,167 --> 00:27:26,967
[GABO] Don't worry, Pops.

609
00:27:26,967 --> 00:27:29,667
I will find them.

610
00:27:30,433 --> 00:27:33,800
I will save those women.

611
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:38,800
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

612
00:27:40,833 --> 00:27:42,033
Gabo.

613
00:27:43,433 --> 00:27:45,867
On your missions,

614
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:52,700
you'll be dealing with forces
so big that even in your dreams,

615
00:27:52,733 --> 00:27:54,900
you won't be able to imagine it.

616
00:27:54,900 --> 00:27:58,767
People who don't
hesitate to take a life.

617
00:27:59,500 --> 00:28:02,033
Cold-blooded killers.

618
00:28:02,767 --> 00:28:04,567
Plagues of society.

619
00:28:04,567 --> 00:28:09,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

620
00:28:09,467 --> 00:28:10,900
Don't be afraid, Gabo.

621
00:28:13,567 --> 00:28:15,900
Don't second-guess.

622
00:28:19,467 --> 00:28:25,667
Anino has been given the power
and license to respond.

623
00:28:25,700 --> 00:28:27,733
And if necessary,

624
00:28:28,467 --> 00:28:29,733
to kill.

625
00:28:30,267 --> 00:28:32,800
And you, Gabo,

626
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:36,033
you are at the end of the line.

627
00:28:36,033 --> 00:28:38,333
You are the blade of the sword.

628
00:28:40,100 --> 00:28:45,733
You are the fist of Anino.

629
00:28:46,267 --> 00:28:53,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

630
00:29:02,300 --> 00:29:05,100
<i>A man broke inside
our boarding house.</i>

631
00:29:05,100 --> 00:29:08,500
<i> He is stealing our underwear!</i>

632
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:09,400
<i> Huh?</i>

633
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:11,533
Alex, where is our destination?

634
00:29:11,533 --> 00:29:13,200
<i> To Emerald Heights, boss.</i>

635
00:29:14,233 --> 00:29:16,900
<i>Misty leaves the house
at this time.</i>

636
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:19,200
<i>She takes a cab
to the clubhouse.</i>

637
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:22,367
<i>She recruits her
female victims there.</i>

638
00:29:22,900 --> 00:29:24,900
<i>You think you can
get away from me?</i>

639
00:29:24,900 --> 00:29:27,533
<i>I'll follow you
everywhere you go!</i>
